    "The chunk's work is committed on branch c41-api at HEAD (the pre-gate commit 70b4a920, the driver fix a12d20a8 and the first-native-run fixes 65f141f4: a save's word gives way to Unsaved changes on the next edit, the request tree stacks above the editor below 760px, the driver returns to the list request's tab before the keyboard send; and the second-run fixes: the status line's last word (a send's completion too) gives way to Unsaved changes on the next edit, the title row's chips shrink instead of widening the row at 200%; and the third-run fix: the view follows the core's tab selection only when it changes, so a snapshot from before + no longer re-opens the previous request over the new draft (the core then selected it again); and the attempt-01 remediation abc05a3b (docs/planning/reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-01.md): following the selection is scoped to the open collection, the request tree is a hierarchy with descendant counts, a tool sheet returns focus to the Collection chip through Modal's explicit returnFocus, every edit settles the status line, and native N01 asserts the keyboard open/close focus return; BASE_REF=73048f76) in its own worktree branched from C40's commit 73048f76 (on c40-cases, itself from C39b's 49a5bac1, C39a's 640103e7 and main's C38 1ff6fe17), so the earlier chunks' gates stayed in scope; scope and diff.patch are measured from 73048f76. The owner's uncommitted build files (xtask sources, Cargo.lock, the Tauri manifests, the desktop-core version bump, the harness pin, the legacy feature views) are present as uncommitted copies, excluded from scope as the owner's work; the v2 API Client imports none of the legacy views (WorkbenchView and the legacy editor are not imported; the text helpers in workbench-call.ts are shared). Native acceptance C41-N01..N02 recorded against the rebuilt fixture bundle (native-prepare.json; executable hash bound in native-acceptance.json) with AX trees, self-captures and the measured layout matrix under evidence/C41/screens, against a plain-HTTP loopback service for the collection's requests. The owner's dependency amendment of 2026-10-30 applies (approved in the owner's words, \"Dependency amendment approved\"): P09 chunks are reviewed on their own worktrees from each predecessor's pre-gate commit; predecessor remediation is integrated by the merge chain and validated by the P09 phase review, so a chunk's review takes the predecessor's record as it stands.",
