| R2 folders rendered flat: collapsing one hid only its direct requests, and a folder counted none of its descendants | The tree is a hierarchy: every folder (listed, implied by a request's path or by a deeper folder) has its child folders and its direct requests under it; a collapsed folder hides its whole subtree; a folder's count is every request under it (the prototype's `visible(parent)` walk and descendant counts). Search still lists matches flat, collapsed or not. Test: nested `products/runtime` under `products`, counts 2 and 1, collapsing the parent hides the child folder and both requests, search finds the nested request, collapsing the child alone hides only its request | `request-tree.tsx`, `api-client.test.tsx` |
